1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,960
Busan stretches a long way along the coast

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:04,900
so trying to cross the whole city in one

3
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:06,540
day can eat up your time.

4
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:08,540
This plan stays on the east side

5
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:09,440
where the sea

6
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:11,760
the beach and your afternoon spa are all part

7
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:13,040
of one easy route.

8
00:00:13,602 --> 00:00:17,662
Begin at a Buddhist temple perched above the water.

9
00:00:17,662 --> 00:00:20,882
Then head back toward Haeundae for a beach walk

10
00:00:20,882 --> 00:00:22,762
a casual lunch and, later

11
00:00:22,762 --> 00:00:25,742
a slow afternoon in a Korean spa.

12
00:00:25,742 --> 00:00:27,022
It is a full day

13
00:00:27,022 --> 00:00:29,382
but the stops make sense together.

14
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:31,829
The day ends back by the sea.

15
00:00:31,829 --> 00:00:34,016
Have dinner near Haeundae Beach

16
00:00:34,016 --> 00:00:37,181
then enjoy the shoreline after dark or take a

17
00:00:37,181 --> 00:00:40,346
short taxi ride to Gwangalli Beach for a view

18
00:00:40,346 --> 00:00:42,660
of the lit-up Gwangan Bridge.

19
00:00:43,254 --> 00:00:46,354
Here is the route at a glance:

20
00:00:46,354 --> 00:00:48,474
start at Haedong Yonggungsa

21
00:00:48,474 --> 00:00:51,814
return to Haeundae for the beach and market

22
00:00:51,814 --> 00:00:53,834
continue to Centum City for the spa

23
00:00:53,834 --> 00:00:55,694
then come back for dinner.

24
00:00:55,694 --> 00:00:58,134
The order keeps your day focused on one side

25
00:00:58,134 --> 00:00:58,854
of Busan.

26
00:00:59,616 --> 00:01:03,096
Let’s make one day in Busan feel straightforward

27
00:01:03,096 --> 00:01:05,436
with a clear route

28
00:01:05,436 --> 00:01:07,796
realistic travel advice and a few good choices

29
00:01:07,796 --> 00:01:09,676
if you have extra time.

30
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:14,130
A little planning makes this route much easier.

31
00:01:14,130 --> 00:01:16,170
The biggest decision is whether you are

32
00:01:16,170 --> 00:01:20,230
sleeping in Busan or arriving from Seoul

33
00:01:20,230 --> 00:01:23,130
because the temple and Haeundae are not near

34
00:01:23,130 --> 00:01:24,250
Busan Station.

35
00:01:24,876 --> 00:01:26,656
Coming from Seoul

36
00:01:26,656 --> 00:01:29,556
the KTX from Seoul Station to Busan Station

37
00:01:29,556 --> 00:01:32,736
takes about two and a half hours.

38
00:01:32,736 --> 00:01:34,376
From Busan Station

39
00:01:34,376 --> 00:01:36,596
allow about an hour by subway

40
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:38,796
changing from Line One to Line Two

41
00:01:38,796 --> 00:01:41,456
or stay near Haeundae the night before.

42
00:01:41,742 --> 00:01:43,002
For this plan

43
00:01:43,002 --> 00:01:45,862
staying near Haeundae is a practical choice

44
00:01:45,862 --> 00:01:49,122
especially if you want to start early at the temple.

45
00:01:49,122 --> 00:01:51,262
If you are taking the KTX down and back

46
00:01:51,262 --> 00:01:52,682
in one day

47
00:01:52,682 --> 00:01:54,102
know that it is possible

48
00:01:54,102 --> 00:01:55,902
but it makes for a long day.

49
00:01:56,208 --> 00:01:59,075
The transit card you use in Seoul also works

50
00:01:59,075 --> 00:02:00,828
on Busan subways and buses.

51
00:02:00,828 --> 00:02:03,217
Bring the same card if you have one

52
00:02:03,217 --> 00:02:05,819
and check current routes in Naver Map or

53
00:02:05,819 --> 00:02:08,668
KakaoMap before you leave for each stop.

54
00:02:09,066 --> 00:02:12,325
Check opening hours on a map app on the day

55
00:02:12,325 --> 00:02:15,584
especially for SPA LAND and the Blueline Park.

56
00:02:15,584 --> 00:02:17,480
In summer and on weekends

57
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:19,851
sky capsule tickets can sell out

58
00:02:19,851 --> 00:02:22,636
so book ahead if that ride is part of

59
00:02:22,636 --> 00:02:23,706
your plan.

60
00:02:24,276 --> 00:02:26,976
This is the route for your day:

61
00:02:26,976 --> 00:02:27,916
temple first

62
00:02:27,916 --> 00:02:30,516
then Haeundae Beach and its nearby market

63
00:02:30,516 --> 00:02:33,376
followed by SPA LAND in Centum City.

64
00:02:33,376 --> 00:02:35,396
Finish back near the beach for dinner.

65
00:02:35,396 --> 00:02:36,076
Start early

66
00:02:36,076 --> 00:02:38,436
and use a taxi for the temple if you

67
00:02:38,436 --> 00:02:39,796
want the simplest trip.

68
00:02:40,086 --> 00:02:43,024
The route map keeps the day in visit order.

69
00:02:43,024 --> 00:02:45,961
The morning trip north to the temple is the

70
00:02:45,961 --> 00:02:46,848
longest move;

71
00:02:46,848 --> 00:02:47,624
after that

72
00:02:47,624 --> 00:02:48,843
the beach, market

73
00:02:48,843 --> 00:02:51,448
spa and dinner fit into a more compact

74
00:02:51,448 --> 00:02:52,746
east-side plan.

75
00:02:53,088 --> 00:02:55,809
Start at Haedong Yonggungsa in Gijang

76
00:02:55,809 --> 00:02:59,256
a Buddhist temple built on rocks above the sea.

77
00:02:59,256 --> 00:03:02,158
It is one of the few Korean temples on

78
00:03:02,158 --> 00:03:05,181
the shoreline instead of in the mountains.

79
00:03:05,181 --> 00:03:05,907
Go early

80
00:03:05,907 --> 00:03:08,928
because it gets busy from mid-morning.

81
00:03:09,354 --> 00:03:12,394
Allow about an hour at the temple.

82
00:03:12,394 --> 00:03:14,614
There are steps down to the main hall

83
00:03:14,614 --> 00:03:16,654
so take your time.

84
00:03:16,654 --> 00:03:18,754
This is a place of worship:

85
00:03:18,754 --> 00:03:19,954
keep your voice low

86
00:03:19,954 --> 00:03:23,054
and be considerate when taking photos.

87
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:26,054
A taxi from Haeundae to the temple takes

88
00:03:26,054 --> 00:03:28,066
around twenty to thirty minutes

89
00:03:28,066 --> 00:03:29,389
depending on traffic.

90
00:03:29,389 --> 00:03:30,766
Local buses also run.

91
00:03:30,766 --> 00:03:33,889
Check the current route in Naver Map or KakaoMap

92
00:03:33,889 --> 00:03:36,536
and show the driver the name on your map

93
00:03:36,536 --> 00:03:38,160
app if you need to.

94
00:03:38,670 --> 00:03:42,110
Head back to Haeundae Beach for a walk on

95
00:03:42,110 --> 00:03:44,630
the sand and the promenade.

96
00:03:44,630 --> 00:03:46,970
Summer weekends can be very busy

97
00:03:46,970 --> 00:03:49,410
so an early start helps.

98
00:03:49,410 --> 00:03:51,290
Keep the beach for late morning

99
00:03:51,290 --> 00:03:53,450
after your quieter visit to the temple.

100
00:03:53,832 --> 00:03:56,472
For an easy lunch stop

101
00:03:56,472 --> 00:03:58,612
walk into the streets behind the beach and

102
00:03:58,612 --> 00:04:00,932
visit Haeundae Traditional Market.

103
00:04:00,932 --> 00:04:02,832
It is close to the sand and is a

104
00:04:02,832 --> 00:04:05,232
handy place to pick up snacks such as fish

105
00:04:05,232 --> 00:04:06,692
cakes and tteokbokki.

106
00:04:07,242 --> 00:04:08,577
If you have time

107
00:04:08,577 --> 00:04:11,853
the Haeundae Blueline Park runs a beach train

108
00:04:11,853 --> 00:04:15,676
and small sky capsules along the old coastal railway

109
00:04:15,676 --> 00:04:19,620
between Mipo near the end of the beach and Cheongsapo.

110
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:22,229
Tickets can sell out at busy times

111
00:04:22,229 --> 00:04:25,502
so book ahead in summer and on weekends.

112
00:04:25,812 --> 00:04:27,232
In the afternoon

113
00:04:27,232 --> 00:04:31,612
take Line Two one stop from Haeundae to Centum City.

114
00:04:31,612 --> 00:04:34,172
SPA LAND is inside Shinsegae Centum City

115
00:04:34,172 --> 00:04:35,412
department store

116
00:04:35,412 --> 00:04:38,532
with hot-spring baths and themed rest rooms.

117
00:04:38,532 --> 00:04:41,012
It is a comfortable introduction to Korean

118
00:04:41,012 --> 00:04:42,252
bathhouse culture.

119
00:04:42,630 --> 00:04:46,110
The spa and department store are in the same building

120
00:04:46,110 --> 00:04:48,790
so you can also shop there or spend longer

121
00:04:48,790 --> 00:04:51,270
indoors if the weather is poor.

122
00:04:51,270 --> 00:04:53,710
Check the spa’s opening hours before you go

123
00:04:53,710 --> 00:04:56,590
and look up basic bathhouse rules if this is

124
00:04:56,590 --> 00:04:58,090
your first Korean spa.

125
00:04:59,088 --> 00:05:02,068
Return to Haeundae for dinner.

126
00:05:02,068 --> 00:05:04,388
Ribs of Legend Haeundae is close to the beach

127
00:05:04,388 --> 00:05:07,348
and serves Korean grilled ribs.

128
00:05:07,348 --> 00:05:08,088
Afterward

129
00:05:08,088 --> 00:05:09,408
walk along the shoreline at night

130
00:05:09,408 --> 00:05:12,828
or take a short taxi ride to Gwangalli Beach.

131
00:05:13,194 --> 00:05:14,205
At Gwangalli

132
00:05:14,205 --> 00:05:17,301
the Gwangan Bridge is lit up after dark.

133
00:05:17,301 --> 00:05:20,081
If you have more time and a car or

134
00:05:20,081 --> 00:05:21,029
taxi budget

135
00:05:21,029 --> 00:05:24,504
Waveon Coffee is a well-known sea-view cafe on

136
00:05:24,504 --> 00:05:25,831
the Gijang coast

137
00:05:25,831 --> 00:05:27,221
north of Haeundae.

138
00:05:27,221 --> 00:05:30,506
The west side of Busan is better saved for

139
00:05:30,506 --> 00:05:31,754
another day.

140
00:05:32,052 --> 00:05:34,745
You do not need to plan a complicated

141
00:05:34,745 --> 00:05:36,852
cross-city route for this day.

142
00:05:36,852 --> 00:05:39,954
The main transfer is from Haeundae to Centum

143
00:05:39,954 --> 00:05:41,242
City on Line Two

144
00:05:41,242 --> 00:05:42,296
just one stop.

145
00:05:42,296 --> 00:05:44,872
The longer trip is the temple visit

146
00:05:44,872 --> 00:05:46,752
north-east of Haeundae.

147
00:05:47,214 --> 00:05:49,394
For Haedong Yonggungsa

148
00:05:49,394 --> 00:05:51,834
a taxi is the simplest option from Haeundae

149
00:05:51,834 --> 00:05:54,134
and takes around twenty to thirty minutes

150
00:05:54,134 --> 00:05:56,154
depending on traffic.

151
00:05:56,154 --> 00:05:57,894
Local buses also run

152
00:05:57,894 --> 00:06:00,554
but check the current route before setting out.

153
00:06:01,032 --> 00:06:05,292
Use Naver Map or KakaoMap for current bus and

154
00:06:05,292 --> 00:06:06,492
subway directions.

155
00:06:06,492 --> 00:06:09,472
They are useful for checking the route on the day

156
00:06:09,472 --> 00:06:11,872
but opening hours should also be checked

157
00:06:11,872 --> 00:06:13,432
before you go

158
00:06:13,432 --> 00:06:15,592
especially for the spa and the Blueline Park.

159
00:06:16,050 --> 00:06:18,234
The Seoul transit card you already use works

160
00:06:18,234 --> 00:06:19,676
on Busan’s subways and buses.

161
00:06:19,676 --> 00:06:21,819
Keep it handy for the ride between Haeundae

162
00:06:21,819 --> 00:06:22,644
and Centum City

163
00:06:22,644 --> 00:06:24,869
and avoid adding extra city crossings that do

164
00:06:24,869 --> 00:06:26,570
not fit this east-coast day.

165
00:06:26,748 --> 00:06:31,588
A few small choices can make this day feel rushed.

166
00:06:31,588 --> 00:06:33,548
Keep these common planning mistakes in mind

167
00:06:33,548 --> 00:06:36,708
before you leave your hotel or book an extra activity.

168
00:06:37,206 --> 00:06:39,246
Watch out for these four things:

169
00:06:39,246 --> 00:06:41,986
starting late at the temple

170
00:06:41,986 --> 00:06:44,866
treating a Seoul day trip as an easy outing

171
00:06:44,866 --> 00:06:46,626
forgetting to check current hours

172
00:06:46,626 --> 00:06:49,466
and leaving popular sky capsule tickets until

173
00:06:49,466 --> 00:06:50,606
the last minute.

174
00:06:51,456 --> 00:06:54,560
Starting early matters because the temple gets

175
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:56,055
busy from mid-morning.

176
00:06:56,055 --> 00:06:58,986
A day trip from Seoul is possible by KTX

177
00:06:58,986 --> 00:07:01,056
but it makes for a long day.

178
00:07:01,056 --> 00:07:02,723
Check hours on the day

179
00:07:02,723 --> 00:07:05,827
and book sky capsules ahead in summer and on

180
00:07:05,827 --> 00:07:08,196
weekends if you want to ride.

181
00:07:08,562 --> 00:07:11,962
Here are quick answers to four useful questions:

182
00:07:11,962 --> 00:07:14,122
can you come from Seoul for the day

183
00:07:14,122 --> 00:07:16,882
what is the easiest way to reach the temple

184
00:07:16,882 --> 00:07:18,762
does the plan work in rain

185
00:07:18,762 --> 00:07:20,762
and where should you stay for this route?

186
00:07:21,228 --> 00:07:24,508
Can you visit from Seoul in one day?

187
00:07:24,508 --> 00:07:25,328
Yes.

188
00:07:25,328 --> 00:07:27,388
The KTX makes it possible

189
00:07:27,388 --> 00:07:29,928
but the return journey and this full itinerary

190
00:07:29,928 --> 00:07:32,128
make for a long day.

191
00:07:32,128 --> 00:07:33,888
You will see more if you stay at least

192
00:07:33,888 --> 00:07:35,148
one night

193
00:07:35,148 --> 00:07:36,648
ideally near Haeundae.

194
00:07:37,686 --> 00:07:40,916
What is the easiest way to reach Haedong Yonggungsa?

195
00:07:40,916 --> 00:07:42,583
Take a taxi from Haeundae.

196
00:07:42,583 --> 00:07:45,083
It takes around twenty to thirty minutes

197
00:07:45,083 --> 00:07:46,385
depending on traffic.

198
00:07:46,385 --> 00:07:48,052
Local buses also go there

199
00:07:48,052 --> 00:07:51,686
and Naver Map or KakaoMap can show the current route.

200
00:07:52,056 --> 00:07:53,963
Does this plan work on a rainy day?

201
00:07:53,963 --> 00:07:54,353
Partly.

202
00:07:54,353 --> 00:07:56,131
The temple and beach are outdoors

203
00:07:56,131 --> 00:07:58,775
but SPA LAND and Shinsegae Centum City are indoors.

204
00:07:58,775 --> 00:08:00,032
If the weather is poor

205
00:08:00,032 --> 00:08:02,196
you can stretch the afternoon there.

206
00:08:02,370 --> 00:08:04,170
Where should you stay?

207
00:08:04,170 --> 00:08:05,710
For this itinerary

208
00:08:05,710 --> 00:08:07,950
stay near Haeundae if you can.

209
00:08:07,950 --> 00:08:10,430
It makes an early temple start easier and

210
00:08:10,430 --> 00:08:12,430
keeps you close to the beach

211
00:08:12,430 --> 00:08:15,330
market and evening dinner after your visit to

212
00:08:15,330 --> 00:08:15,990
Centum City.

213
00:08:16,332 --> 00:08:19,712
The simple version is this:

214
00:08:19,712 --> 00:08:22,292
start early at Haedong Yonggungsa

215
00:08:22,292 --> 00:08:24,432
spend late morning around Haeundae Beach and

216
00:08:24,432 --> 00:08:25,992
its market

217
00:08:25,992 --> 00:08:28,572
take a slow afternoon at SPA LAND

218
00:08:28,572 --> 00:08:30,672
then return to the sea for dinner.

219
00:08:30,990 --> 00:08:34,250
Keep the route on Busan’s east side.

220
00:08:34,250 --> 00:08:37,270
Use a taxi or check local buses for the temple

221
00:08:37,270 --> 00:08:38,790
use your transit card on the subway

222
00:08:38,790 --> 00:08:41,310
and check opening hours and sky capsule

223
00:08:41,310 --> 00:08:43,470
tickets before you go.

224
00:08:43,470 --> 00:08:46,230
Stay near Haeundae if you want an easier start.

225
